# A mixture fraction distributed as beta(1.2, 1.8), of mean 0.4 and variance
# 0.06, mixed by IEM with a reaction too fast for A and B to coexist. Every
# fluid element relaxes to the mean at omega = Cphi/2 epsilon/k = 0.25 1/s:
# xi(t) = 0.4 + (xi(0) - 0.4) exp(-omega t). What A and B are made of is linear
# in the mixture fraction and mixes as it does, so an element holds the product
# of the complete reaction of the two streams mixed at its mixture fraction,
# 0.2 min(xi, 1 - xi), and the mean is its integral over the beta distribution
# of xi(0), found here with the midpoint rule on 1e5 intervals of theta, xi(0)
# = sin^2(theta). The means of the reactants follow: 0.04 - Y_P/2 for A and
# 0.06 - Y_P/2 for B. At time zero the elements have reacted already.
# t [s]   mean Y_P   mean Y_A   mean Y_B
